## how the model-block guard counts 'a row with a value' (CTO half condition 1)
dossier fields['model_rows'] is a list of row dicts {mnemonic|label, source, figure}; figure is {value, unit, source, stamp, fiscal_year|fiscal_period} or {value: null, absent: <reason>}. A row has a value when row['figure']['value'] is not None; a model_rows that is not a list (the {value: null, absent: ...} shape) counts 0. The two counts (served, new) are printed per name in the manifest line and in the GUARD line. The record is dossier._model_block_read(name, client) read again by the driver; its object key must equal the model_block input of the build.

